{"title":"2019 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 3a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_3a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Michelle calculates the average of the following numbers: \n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/2/d6202a123b667bf1273cfdd002dbd7b8c17cbc9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5, 10, 15, 16, 24, 28, 33, 37$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"17\" /></center>\n<p>Daphne removes one number and calculates the average of the remaining numbers. The average that Daphne calculates is one less than the average that Michelle calculates. Which number does Daphne remove?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_3a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The average of the original set is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/d/67ddf7998871baa4f865ec711db9ba15f772b5b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5+10+15+16+24+28+33+37}{8}=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"340\" height=\"38\" />, so the new average must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bb9e41e1ede2020ba55899e127ff45405b750ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21-1=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. Because the original sum of the numbers was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c7116bbc884d2cf49e25754864ae00d9c42d2d90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$168$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> and the new sum of the numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/0/7c0fdf117c488fb64ea36abd673077b705c0b775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\times 7=140$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />, the number taken off must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/b/8bb349a59ae5497f527088a6f5c1044c2e024b51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$168-140=\\boxed{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"132\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~originally by Yuhao2012 and slightly modified by anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018010929\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 30/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1130/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.848      1 2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_3\n100.00%    5.848      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35914:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018010929 and revision id 279210. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}